 has a persistent SHA-256 baseline for /etc and a working checker that directly demonstrated change reporting and clean restoration. Restart evidence is complete: it includes pre-restart identity and health, acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered crond, checker, and unchanged baseline state; fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Removed-file detection was not directly exercised, although the manifest-diff implementation supports it and added-file and modified-file behavior were directly demonstrated.","The lifecycle failed-service probe used systemctl and was unsupported on Alpine; crond health was nevertheless checked directly before and after restart.","The retained effects, if any, of the APK index refresh were not captured in enough detail to determine complete cleanup."]}
